}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3})+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}+{x}_{3}))+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}+{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2})+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group ${x}_{2}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{2},$ factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{2}^{2},$ and complete the square inside the second parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3})-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+([{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3}^{2}]-{x}_{3}^{2})-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}-2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-94162" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Devel