missing from the blank spaces?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-94179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3})+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-{x}_{3}))+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2})+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+7{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group ${x}_{2}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{2},$ factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{2}^{2},$ and complete the square inside the second parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2({x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3})+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2([{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{3}^{2}]-4{x}_{3}^{2})+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2(({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}-4{x}_{3}^{2})+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}-8{x}_{3}^{2}+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-94179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b6f09b463c02a4d9a4b7377799c904ba361482b06139c09001341d7c2129713f"} {"question" "q-94179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-94179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-94179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-94161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-94161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3})-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}(5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}))-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}(5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})+(5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-(5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2})-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-(5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-25{x}_{2}^{2}+10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2}-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-94161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b6f09b463c02a4d9a4b7377799c904ba361482b06139c09001341d7c2129713f"} {"question" "q-94161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-94161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,2{x}_{2}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,2{x}_{2}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,5{x}_{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-94161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-94159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+18{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-94159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+18{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{3})-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+18{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}))-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+18{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-4{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}-4{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-4{x}_{3})^{2})-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+18{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-4{x}_{3})^{2}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+18{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-16{x}_{3}^{2}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+18{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-94159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b6f09b463c02a4d9a4b7377799c904ba361482b06139c09001341d7c2129713f"} {"question" "q-94159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-94159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,2{x}_{2}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,4{x}_{2}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,2{x}_{2}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-94159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-140986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+40{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}+8{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-140986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+40{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{3})-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+40{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-6{x}_{3}))-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+40{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-6{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}-6{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-6{x}_{3})^{2})-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+40{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-6{x}_{3})^{2}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+40{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+12{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-36{x}_{3}^{2}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+40{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group ${x}_{2}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{2},$ factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{2}^{2},$ and complete the square inside the second parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}^{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{3})+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-([{x}_{2}^{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{3}^{2}]-4{x}_{3}^{2})+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}+8{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-140986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b6f09b463c02a4d9a4b7377799c904ba361482b06139c09001341d7c2129713f"} {"question" "q-140986" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-140986" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$"] ["text" "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-6{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "q-140986" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/state.json" "file_sha256" "16d7a5a136fc6fafd30faf10a94b7a24f4dbc353af173196a04d953b37df0e66"} {"question" "e-8184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following quadratic forms are given in their canonical forms?\n\n- $P(\\mathbf{x})=x_1^2-2x_2x_3+x_3^2$\n\n- $Q(\\mathbf{x})=\\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\mathbf{x},$ where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/assets/d041c39fe285ee5fdbd8022b70a8043a4ff07cbeb1dae8c49905248df1b86d01.png)\n\n- $R(\\mathbf{x})=x_3^2-2x_1^2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/example-8184.json" "file_sha256" "2261b6c8de8032db9f66929c2b471c728c9ced34d186c4fed34f73831e6057e5"} {"question" "e-8184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A quadratic form in its canonical form shouldn't contain any cross-product terms ($x_i x_j$ where $i \\neq j$). In terms of its matrix representation, this means that the corresponding matrix is diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our quadratic forms in turn.\n\n- $P(\\mathbf{x})$ is *not* in canonical form since it contains the cross-product term $2x_2x_3.$\n\n- $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ is in canonical form. Indeed, its corresponding matrix is diagonal.\n\n- $R(\\mathbf{x})$ is in canonical form. Indeed, the form does not contain any cross-product terms (it contains only squares).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q(\\mathbf{x})$ and $R(\\mathbf{x})$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/example-8184.json" "file_sha256" "2261b6c8de8032db9f66929c2b471c728c9ced34d186c4fed34f73831e6057e5"} {"question" "e-8185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf{x})=9x_1^2-18x_1x_2+5x_2^2$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/assets/cc77cb76fcab6bd72211e7e66d5fee5ba87c0ba1465571aa88baf26beb196a22.png)\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/example-8185.json" "file_sha256" "22b7ba9df28443193fdab5ad009518c2923f1b72ceb4e1a3c38e278d78f72075"} {"question" "e-8185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group $x_1^2$-term with all cross-product terms that contain $x_1$ and factor out the coefficient of $x_1^2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =9{x}_{1}^{2}-18{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+5{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(9{x}_{1}^{2}-18{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+5{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+5{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+5{x}_{2}^{2} & =9([{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}]-{x}_{2}^{2})+5{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})+5{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})+5{x}_{2}^{2} & =9({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-9{x}_{2}^{2}+5{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/assets/e1048614ed3dda333597bf32339f23a1585308e630233e3d11751c48c597ed52.png)\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\qquad$ $4 \\quad$ and $\\quad x_1-x_2 .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/example-8185.json" "file_sha256" "22b7ba9df28443193fdab5ad009518c2923f1b72ceb4e1a3c38e278d78f72075"} {"question" "e-8186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf{x})=x_1^2-4x_3^2+2x_1x_2-4x_1x_3+2x_2x_3$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/assets/bf0297b0d758d02198d01565050bc5f3b02b0964336d3b84fdca331fabed6051.png)\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/example-8186.json" "file_sha256" "8cfc2204f185257c5ee03969b0b84aaa79aaa3034a4b54292b3ade87408f86d3"} {"question" "e-8186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group $x_1^2$-term with all cross-product terms that contain $x_1$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{3}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3})+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}))+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2})+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-4{x}_{3}^{2}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-8{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group $x_2^2$-term with all cross-product terms that contain $x_2,$ factor out the coefficient of $x_2^2,$ and complete the square inside the second parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{2}{x}_{3})-8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-([{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+9{x}_{3}^{2}]-9{x}_{3}^{2})-8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-3{x}_{3})^{2}+9{x}_{3}^{2}-8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-3{x}_{3})^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/assets/84f88cbb41e573d7ed0793919e0ad25477a46637d09144ca9f462e12f0bc6e90.png)\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\qquad$ $x_1+x_2-2x_3 \\quad$ and $\\quad x_2-3x_3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073449/example-8186.json" "file_sha256" "8cfc2204f185257c5ee03969b0b84aaa79aaa3034a4b54292b3ade87408f86d3"}] "usage" {"e-8184" [] "e-8185" [] "q-94142" [] "e-8186" []} "basis" 2690 "retractions" [[17592186162546 :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x) = 3x_{1}^{2} + 29x_{2}^{2} + 18x_{1}x_{2}$ to the canonical form given below.\n\n$3y_{1}^{2} + 2y_{2}^{2}, {y_{1} = x_{1} + 3x_{2}; y_{2} = x_{2}$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?"] [17592186161718 :question/problem "Which of the following quadratic forms are given in their canonical forms?\n\n1. $P(\\mathbf{x})=x_1^2-2x_2x_3+x_3^2$\n2. $Q(\\mathbf{x})=\\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\mathbf{x}$, where $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\n3. $R(\\mathbf{x})=x_3^2-2x_1^2$"] [17592186161718 :question/worked-solution "A quadratic form in its canonical form shouldn't contain any cross-product terms ($x_i x_j$ where\n\n$$\ni \\neq j\n$$\n\n). In terms of its matrix representation, this means that the corresponding matrix is diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our quadratic forms in turn.\n\n- $P(\\mathbf{x})$ is *not* in canonical form since it contains the cross-product term $2x_2x_3$.\n- $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ is in canonical form. Indeed, its corresponding matrix is diagonal.\n- $R(\\mathbf{x})$ is in canonical form. Indeed, the form does not contain any cross-product terms (it contains only squares).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q(\\mathbf{x})$ and $R(\\mathbf{x})$ only.\""] [17592186161719 :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf{x})=9x_1^2-18x_1x_2+5x_2^2$ to the canonical form given below.\n\n$4$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?"] [17592186161719 :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group $x_1^2$-term with all cross-product terms that contain $x_1$ and factor out the coefficient of $x_1^2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ(x) &= 9x_{1}^{2} - 18x_{1}x_{2} + 5x_{2}^{2} \\\\\n&= (9x_{1}^{2} - 18x_{1}x_{2}) + 5x_{2}^{2} \\\\\n&= 9(x_{1}^{2} - 2x_{1}x_{2}) + 5x_{2}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9(x_{1}^{2} - 2x_{1}x_{2}) + 5x_{2}^{2} &= 9([x_{1}^{2} - 2x_{1}x_{2} + x_{2}^{2}] - x_{2}^{2}) + 5x_{2}^{2} \\\\\n&= 9((x_{1} - x_{2})^{2} - x_{2}^{2}) + 5x_{2}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9((x_{1} - x_{2})^{2} - x_{2}^{2}) + 5x_{2}^{2} &= 9(x_{1} - x_{2})^{2} - 9x_{2}^{2} + 5x_{2}^{2} \\\\\n&= 9(x_{1} - x_{2})^{2} - 4x_{2}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y_{1} = x 1 - x 2; y_{2} = x_{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\qquad$ $4 \\quad$ and $\\quad x_1-x_2$."] [17592186161720 :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf{x})=x_1^2-4x_3^2+2x_1x_2-4x_1x_3+2x_2x_3$ to the canonical form given below.\n\n${y_{1} = [math]\\phantom{x_1+x_2-2x_3}[/math]; y_{2} = [math]\\phantom{x_2-3x_3}[/math]; y_{3} = x_{3}$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?"] [17592186161720 :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group $x_1^2$-term with all cross-product terms that contain $x_1$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ(x) &= x_{1}^{2} - 4x_{3}^{2} + 2x_{1}x_{2} - 4x_{1}x_{3} + 2x_{2}x_{3} \\\\\n&= (x_{1}^{2} + 2x_{1}x_{2} - 4x_{1}x_{3}) + 2x_{2}x_{3} - 4x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&= (x_{1}^{2} + 2x_{1}(x_{2} - 2x_{3})) + 2x_{2}x_{3} - 4x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&= (x_{1}^{2} + 2x_{1}(x_{2} - 2x_{3}) + (x_{2} - 2x_{3})^{2} - (x_{2} - 2x_{3})^{2}) + 2x_{2}x_{3} - 4x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&= (x_{1} + x_{2} - 2x_{3})^{2} - (x_{2} - 2x_{3})^{2} + 2x_{2}x_{3} - 4x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&= (x_{1} + x_{2} - 2x_{3})^{2} - x_{2}^{2} + 4x_{2}x_{3} - 4x_{3}^{2} + 2x_{2}x_{3} - 4x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&= (x_{1} + x_{2} - 2x_{3})^{2} - x_{2}^{2} + 6x_{2}x_{3} - 8x_{3}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group $x_2^2$-term with all cross-product terms that contain $x_2$, factor out the coefficient of $x_2^2$, and complete the square inside the second parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ(x) &= (x_{1} + x_{2} - 2x_{3})^{2} - x_{2}^{2} + 6x_{2}x_{3} - 8x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&= (x_{1} + x_{2} - 2x_{3})^{2} - (x_{2}^{2} - 6x_{2}x_{3}) - 8x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&= (x_{1} + x_{2} - 2x_{3})^{2} - ([x_{2}^{2} - 6x_{2}x_{3} + 9x_{3}^{2}] - 9x_{3}^{2}) - 8x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&= (x_{1} + x_{2} - 2x_{3})^{2} - (x_{2} - 3x_{3})^{2} + 9x_{3}^{2} - 8x_{3}^{2} \\\\\n&= (x_{1} + x_{2} - 2x_{3})^{2} - (x_{2} - 3x_{3})^{2} + x_{3}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y_{1} = x 1 + x 2 - 2 x 3; y_{2} = x 2 - 3 x 3; y_{3} = x_{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\qquad$ $x_1+x_2-2x_3 \\quad$ and $\\quad x_2-3x_3$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186160909 17592186160910 17592186160911 17592186160912 17592186160913] "immutable_fields" [[17592186160908 :answer-field/correct] [17592186160908 :answer-field/id] [17592186160908 :answer-field/key] [17592186160908 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
